config PROFILE_ARM64
    prompt "Target profile"
    type choice
    var ROSCONFIG_PROFILE
    value generic "Generic ARM64"
    value profile_raspberry "Raspberry Pi 3/5"
    value profile_switch "Nintendo Switch (Tegra X1)"
    default generic
    depends ARCH=arm64
    help
      Generic builds the architecture-independent ARM64 target.

      Raspberry Pi 3/5 includes firmware, device trees and drivers for both
      boards: SD/SDIO, DWC2, SMSC95xx and RP1 Ethernet, CYW43xx Wi-Fi,
      display, OpenGL and audio. Hardware IDs select the matching driver.
      The pinned Windows 10 BSP source snapshot is included for parity work.
      It also adds the UEFI HTTP boot option in the Boot options menu.

      Nintendo Switch (Tegra X1) builds LiberNT.img as a microSD card with
      a FAT32 boot partition and the NTFS system partition. Hekate's L4T
      Loader starts the Switchroot BL31 and the WinX EDK II UEFI firmware,
      which starts the LiberNT boot manager. These third-party files are
      not in the tree: scripts/prepare_switch_boot.sh (or .cmd) downloads
      them into media/boot/switch/optional, which the image build copies
      onto the boot partition. No Tegra drivers are included yet.
